### 6.7 · attach — dry, then the two **LIVE** phases
Dry: row count per company, nothing fired. `attach-upload` (gate `MRLOAD_APPROVE_FILES_UPLOAD`)
downloads each Drive file (native Google docs exported) and uploads it to HubSpot Files with
retry/back-off (ledger `files_uploaded`). `attach-notes` (gate `MRLOAD_APPROVE_FILE_NOTES_POST`)
creates one note per file and associates it with the company (ledger `file_notes_posted`).
Both are resumable: the ledger skips what is already done.

#!pwsh

Invoke-Ubuntu 'scripts/run_pass1.sh attach-dry'

#!pwsh

Invoke-Ubuntu 'scripts/run_pass1.sh attach-upload' -Live

#!pwsh

Invoke-Ubuntu 'scripts/run_pass1.sh attach-notes' -Live

